      "explanation": "<p>In phenyl methanamine, the lone pair on nitrogen of -NH<sub>2</sub>\ngroup is localised and does not undergoes resonance.\n</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45tmmxy/b672242b-b509-4733-a7db-595f983265b1/44fd7460-e74a-11ec-885c-21e515ff74ea/file-1l45tmmxz.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l45tmmxy/b672242b-b509-4733-a7db-595f983265b1/44fd7460-e74a-11ec-885c-21e515ff74ea/file-1l45tmmxz.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 179 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l45tmmxy/b672242b-b509-4733-a7db-595f983265b1/44fd7460-e74a-11ec-885c-21e515ff74ea/file-1l45tmmxz.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l45tmmxy/b672242b-b509-4733-a7db-595f983265b1/44fd7460-e74a-11ec-885c-21e515ff74ea/file-1l45tmmxz.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45tmmxy/b672242b-b509-4733-a7db-595f983265b1/44fd7460-e74a-11ec-885c-21e515ff74ea/file-1l45tmmxz.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l45tmmxy/b672242b-b509-4733-a7db-595f983265b1/44fd7460-e74a-11ec-885c-21e515ff74ea/file-1l45tmmxz.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l45tmmxy/b672242b-b509-4733-a7db-595f983265b1/44fd7460-e74a-11ec-885c-21e515ff74ea/file-1l45tmmxz.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l45tmmxy/b672242b-b509-4733-a7db-595f983265b1/44fd7460-e74a-11ec-885c-21e515ff74ea/file-1l45tmmxz.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>(B), (C) and (D) are aromatic amines in which lone pair of electrons\nof N-atoms goes in resonance\n(+R effect) with the benzene ring. So, Lewis basicity or donation of\nlone of electrons of these amines will be decreased in comparison to\n(A).\n</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45tqonh/dc165bf3-0d5c-447c-91e6-91a68a3127a9/b58bd8c0-e74a-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tqoni.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l45tqonh/dc165bf3-0d5c-447c-91e6-91a68a3127a9/b58bd8c0-e74a-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tqoni.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 179 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l45tqonh/dc165bf3-0d5c-447c-91e6-91a68a3127a9/b58bd8c0-e74a-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tqoni.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l45tqonh/dc165bf3-0d5c-447c-91e6-91a68a3127a9/b58bd8c0-e74a-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tqoni.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45tqonh/dc165bf3-0d5c-447c-91e6-91a68a3127a9/b58bd8c0-e74a-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tqoni.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l45tqonh/dc165bf3-0d5c-447c-91e6-91a68a3127a9/b58bd8c0-e74a-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tqoni.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l45tqonh/dc165bf3-0d5c-447c-91e6-91a68a3127a9/b58bd8c0-e74a-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tqoni.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l45tqonh/dc165bf3-0d5c-447c-91e6-91a68a3127a9/b58bd8c0-e74a-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tqoni.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>+ I effects of two -CH<sub>3</sub>\ngroups increases electron density on N atom while lone pair of N atom take part in resonance with the benzene ring and decreases electron density on N atom. Both this effect try to compensate each other.\n</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45tukxo/f388b69b-b2b4-4d35-bee0-3111a4965758/21e98bc0-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tukxp.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l45tukxo/f388b69b-b2b4-4d35-bee0-3111a4965758/21e98bc0-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tukxp.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 179 English Explanation 3\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l45tukxo/f388b69b-b2b4-4d35-bee0-3111a4965758/21e98bc0-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tukxp.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l45tukxo/f388b69b-b2b4-4d35-bee0-3111a4965758/21e98bc0-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tukxp.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45tukxo/f388b69b-b2b4-4d35-bee0-3111a4965758/21e98bc0-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tukxp.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l45tukxo/f388b69b-b2b4-4d35-bee0-3111a4965758/21e98bc0-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tukxp.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l45tukxo/f388b69b-b2b4-4d35-bee0-3111a4965758/21e98bc0-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tukxp.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l45tukxo/f388b69b-b2b4-4d35-bee0-3111a4965758/21e98bc0-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tukxp.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>+ I effects of one -CH<sub>3</sub>\ngroups increases electron density on N atom while lone pair of N atom take part in resonance with the benzene ring and decreases electron density on N atom. Both this effect try to compensate each other.</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45tvjj4/0f210748-8338-49d8-bd7c-ece484a8ec51/3ca2fa00-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tvjj5.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l45tvjj4/0f210748-8338-49d8-bd7c-ece484a8ec51/3ca2fa00-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tvjj5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 179 English Explanation 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l45tvjj4/0f210748-8338-49d8-bd7c-ece484a8ec51/3ca2fa00-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tvjj5.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l45tvjj4/0f210748-8338-49d8-bd7c-ece484a8ec51/3ca2fa00-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tvjj5.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45tvjj4/0f210748-8338-49d8-bd7c-ece484a8ec51/3ca2fa00-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tvjj5.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l45tvjj4/0f210748-8338-49d8-bd7c-ece484a8ec51/3ca2fa00-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tvjj5.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l45tvjj4/0f210748-8338-49d8-bd7c-ece484a8ec51/3ca2fa00-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tvjj5.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l45tvjj4/0f210748-8338-49d8-bd7c-ece484a8ec51/3ca2fa00-e74b-11ec-8080-27ec9ee30011/file-1l45tvjj5.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>It has no + I-effect on N-atom to increase electron density on the N atom which was decreased due to lone pair of N atom take part in resonance with the benzene ring.\nSo, A is purely aliphatic 1°-amine. B is aromatic.\n3°-amine with more aliphatic nature (for two -CH<sub>3</sub>\ngroups). C is\naromatic 2°-amine with less aliphatic nature (for one -CH<sub>3</sub>\ngroup).\n<br>D is purely aromatic 1°-amine.\n<br><br>Hence basicity order is A &gt; B &gt; C &gt; D.\n</p>"
